<title>FINLAND: OIP TO ISSUE FIM 150 MLN FIVE-YEAR BOND.</title>
<headline>OIP TO ISSUE FIM 150 MLN FIVE-YEAR BOND.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish OKO-Investointipankki Oy (OIP), part of cooperative banking group OKOBANK , said on Monday it would issue a 150 million markka five-year bond carrying a 4.50 percent coupon.</p>
<p>The issue price will be variable. Annual coupons would be paid on March 25 and the principal would be repaid on March 25 2002. The bond was not collateralised, it said.</p>
<p>The subscription period will be March 25-July 27, it said, adding it would then seek a listing for the bonds on the Helsinki Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
